{title: 491 - In the Hour of Trial}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #491 • PENITENCE • 10.10.11.11}
{lyricist: James Montgomery}
{composer: Spencer Lane}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 491}
{meta: tune PENITENCE}
{meta: meter 10.10.11.11}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/F]In the [Cm/G]hour [Dm/F]of [Em]trial, [F]Jesus, [Bb/F]plead [F]for me,
[Dm/F]Lest by [Cm/G]base [Dm/F]denial [A]I [Adim]depart [A7]from [Dm/A]Thee;
[F7/A]When Thou [Eb/Bb]see'st [Dm/A]me [Bb/F]waver, [Dm/A]with [F/C]a [Dm/A]look [Bb/F]recall,
[Bb]Nor, for [Adim]fear [Bb7/Ab]or [Gm]favor, [Bb]suffer me [F/C]to [Bb]fall.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/F]With forbidden pleasures [Bb/F]would this [F]vain world [Dm/F]charm;
[Dm/F]Or its [Cm/G]sordid [F]treasures [Adim]spread [A7]to work [Dm/A]me [F7]harm;
[F7/A]Bring to [Eb/Bb]my [Bb/F]remembrance [F/C]sad [Eb/Bb]Gethsemane,
[Bb]Or, in [Adim]darker [Gm]semblance, [Bb]cross-crowned Calvary.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/F]Should Thy [Cm/G]mercy [Em]send [F]me [Bb/F]sorrow, [F]toil, and [Dm/F]woe,
[Dm/F]Or should [Cm/G]pain [Dm/F]attend [F/A]me [A]on [Adim]my [A7]path below,
[F7/A]Grant that [Eb/Bb]I [Dm/A]may [Bb/F]never [Dm/A]fail [F/C]Thy [Dm/A]hand [Bb/F]to [Em]see;
[Bb]Grant that [Adim]I [Bb7/Ab]may [Gm]ever [Bb]cast [Dm/A]my [Bb]care [F/C]on [Bb]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
